V8: "[fastapi] Don't catch uncatchable exceptions after deopt" (crbugs
577627207 and 578797805, not public; no CVE listed yet): when a fast API
call threw an uncatchable termination exception and also lazily
deoptimized its caller, a JavaScript try/catch in the caller could catch
and swallow the termination. V8 main commit
e48d942f29260628f7c53783ae5c76d6cd649874, merged on 2026-11-02 to 15.7
(c9f42910b289c0c3434eecac08c0f81517ebed65, for 157; not yet rolled into
the 157 branch) and proposed for 15.6. This is the 15.7 merge, at v8/,
without its test. Drop it once a 157 tag's V8 has it.

diff --git a/v8/src/execution/isolate.cc b/v8/src/execution/isolate.cc
index e72b8f8..b76289f 100644
--- a/v8/src/execution/isolate.cc
+++ b/v8/src/execution/isolate.cc
@@ -3302,6 +3302,7 @@
         break;
       }
       case StackFrame::INTERNAL: {
+        if (!catchable_by_js) break;
         auto code = frame->GcSafeLookupCode();
         if (code->builtin_id() ==
             Builtin::kDeoptimizationEntry_LazyAfterFastCall) {
